  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nBroad high pressure will remain across the Eastern CONUS through\nthe end of the week. This will allow for continued dry\nconditions with well above avg afternoon temperatures and cold \nnighttime temperatures. Radiational cooling will continue to \nallow for 20-30 degree diurnal ranges some days. \n\nLatest ensemble and AI guidance continues to indicate that our\nnext chance for widespread rain will not arrive until late \nSunday or Monday as a potential area of low pressure crosses \nnear New England. There is still a lot of time between now and \nthen and as always a lot can change so as the saying goes, we \nwill wait and see. More seasonable temperatures will likely \narrive by the middle of next week.",
